      "id": 1,
      "text": "Flamengo was founded on 17 November 1895 by rowers at Nestor de Barros's manor on Flamengo Beach, originally a rowing club.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CR_Flamengo",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The club’s first football uniform, nicknamed the “papagaio vintém,” resembled a kite and was introduced in 1912.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CR_Flamengo",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1914 Flamengo won its first Campeonato Carioca wearing a red‑black‑white striped shirt called the “cobra coral.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CR_Flamengo",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first organized supporters group in Brazil, Charanga Rubro‑Negra, formed in 1942 to back Flamengo’s football team.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CR_Flamengo",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Flamengo’s home stadium, Estádio da Gávea, opened in 1938 and can hold about 4,000 fans, serving as the club’s headquarters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CR_Flamengo",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Legendary striker Zico, dubbed the “White Pelé,” helped cement Flamengo’s dominance in Brazil and earned the club three Copa Libertadores titles.",
